# The org brain is a docs hub — no credential should ever land here.
# NOTE: name-based ignores are defense-in-depth only and are POROUS. The
# authoritative gate is a CONTENT secret-scanner (detect-secrets / gitleaks)
# in brain CI — a scanner, not a filename guess, is what actually enforces
# "secrets never stored." See OCR_STANDARD_reconciliationLoop §8.

# ── Secrets & session state ────────────────────────────────────────────────
cookies.txt
*.token
*.key
*.pem
.env
.env.*
secrets.json
doppler.yaml
*.credentials
# credential-value + command-paste scratch shapes (2026-09-03: a
# "! gh secret set CF_ACCESS_CLIENT_ID --re.txt" slipped past extension globs)
\!*
*CLIENT_ID*.txt
*CLIENT_SECRET*.txt
*ACCESS_KEY*.txt
* gh secret set *

# ── Generated artifacts (regenerated, never committed) ──────────────────────
phantom-scan-report.json
conformance-report.json
*conformance-report.json
adr-edge-report.json
*.log
.sync.log

# ── Scratch / drafts (belong in Linear or an out-of-brain archive, not here) ─
Untitled-*
SESSION-LOG.md
PROJECT-STATUS.md

# ── Tooling / local state ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.claude/worktrees/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
